{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_7b09c8a75478:git:commit:3:1","created_at":"2026-11-05 14:46:41","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"system","role":"cli"}},"payload":{"step_name":"git:commit","phase":"3","iteration":1,"result_json":{"hash":"58a8ca1c751ccfefcc6554d998ecadfb5b7ac35f","short_hash":"58a8ca1c","message":"feat(skills): add 5x-issue-resolution skill and orchestrator wiring (plan 217 phase 3)","files":["5x-cli/docs/development/plans/217-explicit-issue-resolution-plan.md","5x-cli/src/harnesses/cursor/5x-orchestrator.mdc","5x-cli/src/harnesses/opencode/5x-orchestrator.md","5x-cli/src/skills/README.md","5x-cli/src/skills/base/5x-issue-resolution/SKILL.tmpl.md","5x-cli/src/skills/base/5x/SKILL.tmpl.md","5x-cli/src/skills/loader.ts","5x-cli/test/fixtures/issue-resolution/resume-matrix.json","5x-cli/test/helpers/issue-delivery-fixtures.ts","5x-cli/test/integration/issue-resolution-recipes.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/commands/harness.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/harnesses/cursor-skills.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/harnesses/opencode-skills.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/skills/issue-resolution-resume-matrix.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/skills/issue-resolution-skill.test.ts","5x-cli/test/unit/skills/loader.test.ts","docs/development/runs/217-explicit-issue-resolution-plan/run_7b09c8a75478/steps.jsonl"]},"head_commit":"58a8ca1c751ccfefcc6554d998ecadfb5b7ac35f","patch_id":"b3072c67bb2cee5af02b4f3038c23cfce510e4d0","diff_summary":{"files_changed":17,"insertions":3460,"deletions":17},"duration_ms":null,"tokens_in":null,"tokens_out":null,"cost_usd":null,"model":null}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_7b09c8a75478:author:next-phase:3:0","created_at":"2026-11-05 14:46:55","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"author","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"author:next-phase","phase":"3","iteration":0,"result_json":{"result":"complete","commit":"58a8ca1c751ccfefcc6554d998ecadfb5b7ac35f","notes":"Phase 3 (W3) of plan 217 is implemented and committed as 58a8ca1c. Lint and typecheck pass. The full suite's only failure was a hardcoded skill count of 7 in test/unit/commands/harness.test.ts. I changed it to 8 and that file plus test/integration/commands/harness.test.ts now pass (88/88). The full suite was not re-run after that fix.\n\nWhat was added:\n- New skill src/skills/base/5x-issue-resolution/SKILL.tmpl.md, with separate native and invoke delegation branches for author and reviewer. It covers Steps 0-5: discovery and resume classification, planning run plus intake, plan and review, implementation run with bind, PR preparation, and the post-merge source refresh, delivery-identity check, reconciliation order and publication. It also has the formats, the 15-outcome table, invariants and recovery.\n- Seven procedures are written as runnable bash blocks headed `# recipe: <name>`: discover-briefs, prepare-pr, refresh-compare, accepted-intervals, compatibility-intervals, classify-delivery and publish-resolution. The integration tests pull these blocks out of the rendered skill and run them, so the tests check the documented text itself.\n- The skill is registered in src/skills/loader.ts and listed in the skills README. The foundation `5x` skill gets a one-sentence pointer and an updated description. Both orchestrator files (OpenCode and Cursor) list the skill. Permission rules are not widened; push, PR, comment and close writes need operator authorization.\n- I checked the record kinds and field names against record-lines.ts and real run records, `.data.implementation_governance.{binding,reviewedRange}` against live `5x run state` output, and every gh flag and `--json` field used against the installed gh 2.101.0 help.\n- Tests: updated skill-list counts in the loader, cursor, opencode and harness command tests. New files: test/unit/skills/issue-resolution-skill.test.ts (four delegation combinations, markers, Refs-only, commands, outcome set, foundation pointer, orchestrator files); test/fixtures/issue-resolution/resume-matrix.json with 42 rows plus its test; test/helpers/issue-delivery-fixtures.ts (temp git repos, run-record builders, a stub `gh` that rejects unknown flags and JSON fields, a stub `5x`); and test/integration/issue-resolution-recipes.test.ts (29 tests on discovery, delivery identity, refresh comparison, publication ordering and PR preparation).\n\nDesign decisions the plan does not cover:\n1. Intake passes only `issue_ref` and `brief_dir`. The CLI fills in `plan_path` and `run_id` from the run; passing `plan_path` explicitly can trigger a plan-path mismatch guard.\n2. The legacy (unbound) path takes the reviewed input commit from `result_json.reviewedCommit` or `result_json.commit_hash` on a reviewer step, and its base from `implementation:pre-author` steps. Current legacy run records do not store the reviewed input, so in practice this path stops with needs_human. The plan allows that.\n3. The accepted-intervals recipe uses the CLI's full exact-correction proof (including architectureDelta, inventory and the carried-claims match), which is stricter than the plan's summary list.\n4. Recipes must be run with bash: zsh's echo would corrupt JSON escapes, so the recipes use printf and pipefail.\n\nThe working tree still shows the run journal (steps.jsonl) as modified after the commit, as it did at the start."},"head_commit":"58a8ca1c751ccfefcc6554d998ecadfb5b7ac35f","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":1106959,"tokens_in":140,"tokens_out":101606,"cost_usd":5.776385000000001,"model":"opus"}}
